                <pb facs="0629" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/3334: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Crane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-03-27T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 27—11:53
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>130. Legation’s 112, March 12, 2 p.m. French have finally yielded. The Chinese
                    Government is very grateful to the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
